d 'XTBETARK': module for computing beta regression with AR(k) errors for proportion/rate outcomes, by joint conditional maximum likelihood, with panel-corrected standard errors
d
d  xtbetark extends betark (if installed) to panel data.  The AR(k)
d component -- the mean equation's autoregressive adjustment,
d jointly estimated with the scale equation and AR coefficients via
d the same recursive conditional likelihood -- works exactly as in
d betark. xtbetark adds the variance-covariance estimator. A
d panel-appropriate sandwich is applied on top of the
d AR(k)-adjusted likelihood, so the correction targets only the
d cross-panel dependence the AR(k) term does not already handle. 
d Two such corrections are available via vce() -- pcse (Beck and
d Katz [1995]) and dk ( Driscoll and Kraay [1998])-- differing in
d whether they include a time-lag smoothing kernel; a third, oim,
d applies no panel correction at all  and provides results
d identical to those produced by betark. 
d
d KW: Beta regression
d KW: autoregressive errors
d KW: panel data
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
f xtbetark.ado
f xtbetark_p.ado
f xtbetark.sthlp
f xtbetark_example.dta
